WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.760
Invoices, meeting minutes, and messages that keep trust.

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.930
This is the video for module 3 of Business Communication.

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:17.330
Money documents are communication too. A vague invoice leads to late payment and arguments. A clear one gets paid faster.

4
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.480
A quotation is your offer, sent before the customer agrees.

5
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.060
An invoice asks for payment, after the order is agreed or delivered.

6
00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:35.010
A receipt proves you were paid. Write the amount in figures and in words, so no one can easily change it.

7
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:48.230
Ifeoma's first invoice said only: Uniforms, 480,000 naira, pay soon. The school bursar could not tell how many uniforms, or when to pay, so she put it aside.

8
00:00:49.480 --> 00:01:07.840
The new invoice has a number, a date and a due date. Each line shows the item, the quantity and the price. 40 pinafores at 6,500 naira is 260,000. 40 shirt and shorts sets at 5,500 is 220,000.

9
00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:15.810
That is 480,000 naira in total, less the 240,000 deposit already paid.

10
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:26.540
The balance is 240,000 naira, due within 7 days, with her bank details. Every number adds up, so the bursar can approve it at once.

11
00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:33.890
The day before payment is due, send a friendly reminder with the invoice number, the amount and the date.

12
00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:41.860
If it is a few days late, be clear. Say it was due, ask when payment will be made, and attach the invoice again.

13
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:49.660
At two weeks late, be firm. Give a date to pay by, or ask them to call today to agree a payment plan.

14
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:59.500
Protect yourself from scams. Fraudsters send fake transfer alerts and fake screenshots. Check your own banking app before releasing goods.

15
00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:08.580
If a supplier suddenly sends new bank details, call them on a number you already have. Never share your OTP, PIN or BVN.

16
00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:14.630
Send a short meeting agenda at least a day before, with a time for each item.

17
00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:26.230
Afterwards, write action minutes, not every word. Record the date, time and place, who was present, what was decided, who will do what by when, and the next meeting date.

18
00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.710
An action without an owner and a deadline usually does not happen.

19
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:43.740
For example, Doose is secretary of a women's farming cooperative in Benue. Her first notes said, we talked about the trade fair, we will see. No decision, no owner, no deadline.

20
00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:54.380
Her new minutes record the decision: take a stand if the fee is confirmed at 60,000 naira or less, agreed by 12 of 14 members.

21
00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:00.810
Each action has a name and a date, and the next meeting is set. Share minutes within 48 hours.

22
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:08.140
For example, Blessing sells baked goods in Warri. A customer's birthday cake arrived squashed.

23
00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:15.940
Listen. Blessing reads the whole message, asks for a photo, and does not argue about the delivery rider.

24
00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:21.860
Apologise. I am truly sorry. Your daughter's cake should have arrived perfect.

25
00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:32.350
Solve. She offers a choice: a refund of 12,500 naira of the 25,000 today, or a fresh cake free of charge.

26
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:41.640
Thank and follow up. She thanks the customer, changes to a sturdier box, and checks in a week later. The customer stays loyal.

27
00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:49.310
A written promise is something the customer plans around. Check your stock, time and cash before you commit.

28
00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:59.290
Instead of, no problem, 500 packs by Friday, say: we can deliver 300 by Friday and the other 200 by Tuesday.

29
00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:13.380
Nigeria's Data Protection Act 2023 sets rules for personal data. Collect only what you need, keep it secure, and never post screenshots showing customers' names or numbers.

30
00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:22.760
And if a delivery will be late, say so early, with the reason and your new plan. Silence and excuses do far more damage.

31
00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:32.480
To remember. A quote is the offer, an invoice asks for payment, a receipt proves it. Number every invoice and show every item.

32
00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:41.400
Check payments yourself. Record decisions with owners and deadlines. And handle complaints with Listen, Apologise, Solve, Thank.

33
00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:57.730
Now practise. Create your invoice and receipt templates and save three payment reminders. Write an agenda and action minutes for a real meeting. And prepare your trust toolkit: a data rule, a complaint reply and a bad-news message.

34
00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.030
Continue with the lessons below.
